# 7. Typography Usage Guidelines

## 7.1 Hero Typography

The homepage hero is one of the most important typographic moments on the website.

The brand headline is:

**Big Ideas, Real Impact.**

Use Cormorant Garamond for the main headline.

Use DM Sans for:

- Supporting introduction
- Explanatory text
- Calls to action
- Navigation
- Supporting information

### Hero Design Principles

- Establish a strong visual hierarchy between the headline and supporting copy.
- Allow the headline sufficient space.
- Use deliberate line breaks.
- Avoid unnecessarily long headline lines.
- Ensure the headline remains balanced across screen sizes.
- Avoid excessive font-weight variation.
- Maintain strong contrast against the background.
- Do not use excessive decorative typography effects.

The hero should feel like an editorial introduction to an experienced executive leader.

## 7.2 Section Headings

Use Cormorant Garamond for prominent section headings.

Examples include:

- About Me
- Work With Me
- Speaking
- Writing
- Contact Me

Section headings should feel distinctive without becoming visually overwhelming.

Use DM Sans for any supporting section descriptions or introductory paragraphs.

## 7.3 Body Content

Use DM Sans for general content.

This includes:

- Professional biography
- Leadership experience
- Areas of expertise
- Advisory and partnership descriptions
- Professional achievements
- Supporting explanations

### Body Text Principles

- Maintain comfortable reading widths.
- Use appropriate line-height.
- Avoid excessively long paragraphs.
- Break content into meaningful sections.
- Use paragraph spacing to improve scanning.
- Avoid unnecessary bolding and italicisation.
- Maintain consistent text alignment.

## 7.4 Featured Quotes

Use Cormorant Garamond for selected prominent quotations or editorial statements.

Use DM Sans for attribution and supporting details.

Do not create quotations or attribute statements to the client without verified source material.

## 7.5 Navigation and Buttons

Use DM Sans for all navigation and button labels.

Navigation should feel:

- Clear
- Refined
- Compact
- Professional
- Easy to scan

Avoid decorative serif typography for functional navigation elements.

## 7.6 Writing Section

The Writing section should feel like a refined editorial publication.

Use:

- Cormorant Garamond for article and publication titles.
- DM Sans for article descriptions, metadata, dates, categories, and supporting content.

Maintain comfortable reading widths and clear distinctions between titles, summaries, and metadata.

