# 17. Prohibited Typography Practices

The following practices are prohibited:

- Introducing unrelated font families.
- Replacing Cormorant Garamond or DM Sans without approval.
- Using Cormorant Garamond indiscriminately for body content.
- Using DM Sans for every prominent display heading.
- Arbitrary font sizes outside the approved token system.
- Duplicating existing font declarations.
- Creating a competing typography system.
- Excessive font-weight variation.
- Excessive letter spacing.
- Overly decorative text treatments.
- Inconsistent heading hierarchy.
- Excessively long display headlines.
- Unreadable paragraph widths.
- Dense blocks of body text.
- Unnecessary uppercase styling.
- Low-contrast typography.
- Inconsistent typography between sections.
- Fixed-height text containers that clip content.
- Using heading elements solely for their default visual appearance.

The website must preserve a refined, editorial, readable, and consistent typographic identity.

